WEBVTT

00:01.600 --> 00:04.700
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:04.700 --> 00:08.270
My thoughts travel the wilderness

00:08.270 --> 00:16.180
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

00:21.350 --> 00:27.990
Under the scorching rays of the sun,
what thoughts cross your mind?

00:27.990 --> 00:33.900
What does your grief-stricken gaze reflect now?

00:33.900 --> 00:42.840
If I can keep from losing my way,
step by step, it should be easy

00:42.840 --> 00:47.540
Like the wind

00:47.540 --> 00:50.650
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:50.650 --> 00:54.150
I travel the dawn-lit wilderness

00:54.150 --> 01:00.690
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

01:00.690 --> 01:07.430
Don't be afraid, change is
nothing to be frightened of

01:07.430 --> 01:13.570
As long as you are yourself, I will be with you

01:13.570 --> 01:20.240
Dreaming of tranquil days

01:20.240 --> 01:27.550
The roadless journey continues

02:01.720 --> 02:03.210
There!

02:08.890 --> 02:11.830
Give me a break, bonita. ["beautiful"]

02:11.830 --> 02:14.460
Not Bonita. Ellis.

02:14.460 --> 02:18.670
You're an unfamiliar face. Are you on a trip?

02:18.670 --> 02:20.270
We're going south.

02:20.270 --> 02:22.840
South? South where?

02:22.840 --> 02:24.170
I don't know.

02:24.170 --> 02:27.160
You don't know? What's that mean?

02:29.840 --> 02:32.350
Wait... Hold on now...

02:32.350 --> 02:35.650
I'm pretty sure I've seen your face somewhere...

02:37.520 --> 02:39.590
Ellis, thanks for waiting.

02:39.590 --> 02:42.590
Oh, did she cause some kind of trouble?

02:42.590 --> 02:45.430
I'm sorry, she's so naive about this world.

02:45.430 --> 02:46.920
Oh!

02:49.830 --> 02:52.030
So you're the bounty hunter!

02:52.030 --> 02:53.660
Give it up quietly!

02:55.500 --> 02:57.840
Ellis, hang on tight!

03:01.780 --> 03:04.110
- There they are!
- Those bastards!

03:08.120 --> 03:12.390
Whew! That was close!

03:12.390 --> 03:14.050
It's mine now.

03:17.060 --> 03:18.790
I'm happy for you.

03:23.970 --> 03:27.370
Ellis is pure and innocent.

03:36.580 --> 03:39.550
- Oh, man...
- We can't pass.

03:39.550 --> 03:41.310
Yeah.

03:42.920 --> 03:44.490
Can't you do something about it?

03:44.490 --> 03:45.820
Something? Like what?

03:45.820 --> 03:52.030
You know, like Moses. Make it
rumble apart and create a path!

03:52.030 --> 03:54.400
What's Moses?

03:54.400 --> 03:56.990
Never mind. Forget I said anything.

03:58.500 --> 04:00.500
Let's go back for now.

04:00.500 --> 04:02.490
- Rain.
- What?

04:04.670 --> 04:06.210
Whoa...

04:06.210 --> 04:09.010
- This sucks.
- We have no roof.

04:09.010 --> 04:12.580
Ellis, let's get off and
find shelter from the rain.

04:12.580 --> 04:14.070
Yessir.

04:30.200 --> 04:33.570
Name, Josha Clreosky.

04:33.570 --> 04:35.370
Male, age 45.

04:35.370 --> 04:38.110
He was carrying an employee ID card
from Kilroi Medicine Manufacturing,

04:38.110 --> 04:40.100
but it's from 3 years ago.

04:48.420 --> 04:49.950
Rosenberg.

04:49.950 --> 04:52.450
It's done.

04:52.450 --> 04:54.610
Good work.

05:05.000 --> 05:06.830
Let's go there.

05:06.830 --> 05:08.670
Yessir.

05:12.170 --> 05:14.840
Ellis? What's wrong?

05:17.250 --> 05:18.740
Ellis?!

05:24.690 --> 05:28.120
You dummy! What are you doing?!

05:28.120 --> 05:29.950
He came down the river.

05:31.960 --> 05:33.800
A lizard?

05:33.800 --> 05:35.530
You saved him?

05:35.530 --> 05:36.960
Yeah.

05:36.960 --> 05:39.430
Honestly! You are just so...

05:57.120 --> 05:59.850
Whew! Saved!

05:59.850 --> 06:02.390
I wonder if someone lives here...

06:02.390 --> 06:04.380
- There is someone.
- Huh?

06:08.500 --> 06:09.960
Sorry for barging in here.

06:09.960 --> 06:13.020
We couldn't find anywhere
else to get out of the rain.

06:16.140 --> 06:19.810
Uh... um... hello?

06:19.810 --> 06:21.640
Are you asleep?

06:27.980 --> 06:29.320
Asleep.

06:29.320 --> 06:32.150
Yeah, for all eternity.

06:32.150 --> 06:34.690
Get your clothes off, or you'll catch a cold.

06:34.690 --> 06:36.490
Yessir.

06:41.030 --> 06:43.660
We better get that present of yours off, too.

07:00.550 --> 07:02.620
Because you'll catch a cold.

07:02.620 --> 07:04.690
Here.

07:04.690 --> 07:06.090
Coffee.

07:06.090 --> 07:08.960
It'll warm you up.

07:08.960 --> 07:10.090
What about cream?

07:10.090 --> 07:12.860
There wasn't any cream, but I found sugar.

07:12.860 --> 07:13.930
Want some?

07:13.930 --> 07:16.020
- Two.
- Got it.

07:21.540 --> 07:23.200
What about for him?

07:23.200 --> 07:26.110
Lizards don't drink coffee.

07:26.110 --> 07:27.940
Right.

07:29.110 --> 07:30.940
What about that man?

07:34.380 --> 07:37.980
I don't know how far I
should take you seriously.

07:48.160 --> 07:50.390
I guess he had a family.

07:53.400 --> 07:56.740
But he wound up alone here in the end...

07:56.740 --> 07:59.240
I wonder what happened.

07:59.240 --> 08:01.410
Did they all die?

08:01.410 --> 08:03.640
Who knows?

08:03.640 --> 08:05.740
Do you think that's what happened?

08:07.480 --> 08:09.470
I don't really know.

08:12.250 --> 08:14.820
If his family were dead,

08:14.820 --> 08:17.020
I guess that'd be more fortunate for him.

08:17.020 --> 08:19.790
He'd have no regrets that way, too.

08:19.790 --> 08:22.660
But if they're all alive,

08:22.660 --> 08:26.860
and they were living
separately for some reason...

08:32.440 --> 08:37.650
"Someday, my loved ones will
open that door and come back..."

08:37.650 --> 08:41.150
"Someday... Someday, surely."

08:41.150 --> 08:44.950
It'd be painful if he died
with thoughts like that...

08:44.950 --> 08:46.610
What about you, Nadie?

08:49.390 --> 08:52.790
No worries. I'm one of the fortunate ones.

08:52.790 --> 08:54.200
They're all dead already.

08:54.200 --> 08:56.830
- Me, too.
- What?

08:56.830 --> 08:59.800
I'm one of the fortunate ones, too.

08:59.800 --> 09:02.460
Because the Doctor's dead...

09:04.510 --> 09:06.200
Ellis...

09:13.810 --> 09:15.880
Hey, do that thing.

09:15.880 --> 09:17.020
That thing?

09:17.020 --> 09:19.920
The thing you were doing when we met.

09:21.660 --> 09:23.250
Sure.

09:33.170 --> 09:35.260
Come on, clap! Clap!

09:38.740 --> 09:41.410
It's such a strange power.

09:41.410 --> 09:44.410
Do you know about me, Nadie?

09:44.410 --> 09:45.910
Nope.

09:45.910 --> 09:48.850
I caught you because you
were a bounty, that's all.

09:48.850 --> 09:50.720
Am I weird?

09:50.720 --> 09:52.190
Huh?

09:52.190 --> 09:55.860
You're not normal, but you're
not especially weird.

09:55.860 --> 09:58.560
You have a power that's
different from other people.

09:58.560 --> 10:00.530
That's all there is to it.

10:00.530 --> 10:02.060
I see.

10:02.060 --> 10:05.400
I used to think everyone thought I was weird.

10:05.400 --> 10:10.040
Some people will have unpleasant
views on things and some won't.

10:10.040 --> 10:11.710
That's how it is with everything.

10:11.710 --> 10:15.140
So what you do is learn to
ignore the unpleasant side.

10:15.140 --> 10:17.980
That way, you can keep the
painful things from taking over.

10:17.980 --> 10:20.720
That's the trick to making
your way in this world.

10:20.720 --> 10:22.550
Huh.

10:22.550 --> 10:27.590
Oh, hey, how do you make that power work?

10:27.590 --> 10:30.730
If I work hard at it, do you
think I could do it, too?

10:30.730 --> 10:31.960
I don't know.

10:31.960 --> 10:33.660
You don't know, huh?

10:33.660 --> 10:37.830
Well, you can know surprisingly
little about yourself sometimes.

10:37.830 --> 10:39.320
But...

10:54.350 --> 10:57.420
I'm sure this will tell me.

10:57.420 --> 10:59.620
The Inca rose...

10:59.620 --> 11:01.180
Wiñay Ma...

11:07.760 --> 11:09.930
Come on, you're going to catch a cold.

11:09.930 --> 11:11.520
Yessir.

11:44.900 --> 11:46.970
They're close by.

11:46.970 --> 11:49.800
- Let's get them.
- Yes.

11:49.800 --> 11:52.210
But talk about an awful downpour.

11:52.210 --> 11:55.300
I know! It's depressing.

12:16.000 --> 12:18.700
I thought you'd quit long ago.

12:18.700 --> 12:21.570
Well, a lot's happened...

12:21.570 --> 12:24.840
Who's that girl? She's not yours, right?

12:24.840 --> 12:28.840
I've never heard of a bounty
hunter with a kid in tow.

12:28.840 --> 12:32.510
This isn't some Japanese samurai movie.

12:37.550 --> 12:39.620
You quit?

12:39.620 --> 12:43.080
You've cleaned up a lot, haven't you?

12:45.430 --> 12:48.400
I've got a family now, too.

12:48.400 --> 12:51.200
So you're a champion of justice, are you?

12:51.200 --> 12:53.900
But life's gotten tougher because of it.

12:53.900 --> 12:56.570
That's how the world works.

12:56.570 --> 13:00.140
- So?
- Oh, about that bounty I mentioned earlier?

13:00.140 --> 13:02.310
Said they were headed south.

13:02.310 --> 13:03.980
South?

13:03.980 --> 13:07.550
It seems even she doesn't know more than that.

13:07.550 --> 13:11.480
Maybe the woman bounty hunter
who was with her knows.

13:13.220 --> 13:16.560
Is your target that girl named Ellis?

13:16.560 --> 13:18.550
I don't know yet.

13:21.460 --> 13:23.660
Let me give you some friendly advice.

13:23.660 --> 13:26.130
You should wash your hands
of this business soon, too.

13:30.970 --> 13:32.600
Lirio.

13:36.180 --> 13:38.940
The era for putting your
life on the line is over.

13:41.420 --> 13:43.010
Ricardo...

13:54.460 --> 13:57.670
- I guess it could be a bit spicier.
- Open.

13:57.670 --> 13:58.970
Did you get the cans opened?

13:58.970 --> 14:00.660
Ellis!

14:01.970 --> 14:05.170
- Cut.
- Oh, man!

14:05.170 --> 14:07.000
Use this for starters.

14:09.180 --> 14:11.780
Let's see, as for a bandage...

14:11.780 --> 14:14.150
I wonder if there's a
first-aid box or something...

14:43.010 --> 14:45.050
Ellis!

14:45.050 --> 14:48.140
What are you doing? It's bleeding a lot!

14:55.060 --> 14:57.730
I wonder if it's stopped...

14:57.730 --> 14:59.090
Is it tasty?

14:59.090 --> 15:01.400
Is what tasty? The blood?

15:01.400 --> 15:06.100
Like it would be tasty.
I'm not a vampire here.

15:06.100 --> 15:09.770
There. That should do it.

15:09.770 --> 15:11.370
Be careful now.

15:11.370 --> 15:15.680
You may have a strange power,
but you're still human.

15:15.680 --> 15:16.780
Human?

15:16.780 --> 15:19.910
You're human, aren't you?
I mean, you've got red blood.

15:22.680 --> 15:24.170
Right.

15:25.520 --> 15:27.610
Don't say such weird things.

15:30.790 --> 15:32.880
She said I'm human.

15:39.700 --> 15:43.230
- That must be the place.
- Yes, no doubt about it.

15:50.780 --> 15:53.470
- Who are you?!
- Don't get in our way!

16:02.720 --> 16:04.560
H-Hey!

16:04.560 --> 16:06.550
Hold it right there!

16:08.960 --> 16:12.000
It'll be impossible to cross like this.

16:12.000 --> 16:13.830
Let's go back to the car.

16:13.830 --> 16:15.940
We'll hide and lie in wait for them.

16:15.940 --> 16:17.740
I guess we have no choice.

16:17.740 --> 16:19.570
But still...

16:19.570 --> 16:21.580
That brat...

16:21.580 --> 16:23.440
Who in the world?

16:27.080 --> 16:29.450
This may not taste good,

16:29.450 --> 16:32.090
but, well, it's better than not eating.

16:32.090 --> 16:34.620
Okay, come over here...

16:34.620 --> 16:36.110
Ellis!

16:37.160 --> 16:38.460
Put it back.

16:38.460 --> 16:39.960
I'm just looking at it.

16:39.960 --> 16:41.590
Quickly.

16:42.800 --> 16:44.290
Okay.

16:46.470 --> 16:49.670
It's not a toy.

16:49.670 --> 16:52.000
- Are you mad?
- What?

16:55.940 --> 16:58.980
I'm not really mad, but...

16:58.980 --> 17:01.550
Don't touch it again, okay?

17:01.550 --> 17:04.390
All right.

17:04.390 --> 17:07.120
Time to eat.

17:07.120 --> 17:08.950
What's that?

17:10.290 --> 17:12.320
Playing bounty.

17:19.570 --> 17:21.470
Thanks for the food.

17:23.640 --> 17:25.660
Thanks for the food.

17:28.810 --> 17:30.580
What about your, "Thanks for the food"?

17:30.580 --> 17:35.150
"Hah, like I'd bother saying that
when it didn't even taste good."

17:35.150 --> 17:37.320
That's the look he's got on his face.

17:37.320 --> 17:40.220
I guess he's honest.

17:40.220 --> 17:43.590
- Hey, now...
- But it's better than not eating.

17:43.590 --> 17:45.560
No softening the blow, huh?

17:45.560 --> 17:47.660
Well, not that I care.

17:47.660 --> 17:50.230
Okay, Ellis, clean things up.

17:50.230 --> 17:51.530
Why?

17:51.530 --> 17:54.760
I cooked, so you're cleaning up.

17:56.670 --> 17:58.270
Come on, just clean it up.

17:58.270 --> 17:59.900
Yessir.

18:02.110 --> 18:04.180
I heard a sound.

18:04.180 --> 18:05.770
Don't move.

18:21.730 --> 18:23.060
Found them?

18:23.060 --> 18:24.760
There was no one around.

18:30.740 --> 18:33.310
- Nadie...
- She's fine.

18:33.310 --> 18:35.540
She's just passed out.

18:37.610 --> 18:39.240
Ellis.

18:40.580 --> 18:42.550
Who are you?

18:42.550 --> 18:46.050
Right now, it still doesn't matter who I am.

18:46.050 --> 18:51.390
But eventually, I'll become
an important part of your life.

18:51.390 --> 18:53.220
No, you won't.

18:57.500 --> 19:00.270
Who are you? A bounty hunter?

19:00.270 --> 19:05.340
I'll be watching you always.

19:05.340 --> 19:08.400
That's what I came to tell you.

19:23.090 --> 19:26.630
Don't scare me, you dummy.

19:26.630 --> 19:29.100
- Ellis...
- He left.

19:29.100 --> 19:30.830
What?

19:30.830 --> 19:33.470
He said he'll always be watching.

19:33.470 --> 19:35.300
Huh?

19:52.220 --> 19:55.960
Please do not act too much
at your own discretion.

19:55.960 --> 19:59.120
For I would like to be able to trust you.

20:02.630 --> 20:06.160
I am the one who gave you the capacity to feel.

20:08.640 --> 20:10.690
I hope you understand that...

20:17.540 --> 20:19.810
Are you really fine with the chair?

20:19.810 --> 20:22.750
Yeah. It's what I've done for a long time now,

20:22.750 --> 20:24.690
so I sleep better in a chair.

20:24.690 --> 20:26.750
I see.

20:26.750 --> 20:29.660
Okay, good night, Ellis.

20:29.660 --> 20:33.180
Yeah, good night, Nadie.

20:40.400 --> 20:43.840
Hey! Come on, wake up!

20:43.840 --> 20:46.510
The rain's let up.

20:46.510 --> 20:49.340
Oh, you're right. All right, then!

21:02.290 --> 21:04.520
Let Ellis...

21:04.520 --> 21:06.960
...get her rest, please.

21:24.210 --> 21:26.580
Okay, this is goodbye.

21:28.150 --> 21:30.220
No?

21:30.220 --> 21:32.620
No.

21:32.620 --> 21:34.380
All right.

21:37.160 --> 21:40.560
Bye-bye. Take care.

21:41.900 --> 21:44.400
And...

21:44.400 --> 21:46.570
Thank you. You were a great help.

21:46.570 --> 21:48.970
Bye-bye. Take care.

21:56.980 --> 21:59.410
All right, south we go!

21:59.410 --> 22:01.010
Go!

22:21.540 --> 22:24.830
I'll be watching, Ellis.

22:26.770 --> 22:29.280
His name is L.A.

22:29.280 --> 22:32.450
His history...

22:32.450 --> 22:34.280
...is unknown.

22:36.620 --> 22:40.350
Like a neverending summer

22:40.350 --> 22:43.890
Like flowers that never die

22:43.890 --> 22:47.790
Those arms you've wrapped around me

22:47.790 --> 22:55.960
Don't ever let go of me

23:02.210 --> 23:05.710
Even if I try clinging to you

23:05.710 --> 23:11.490
My heart still heeds a different evanescence

23:11.490 --> 23:15.420
Counting the rhythm of time by it

23:15.420 --> 23:19.560
A night of red stars

23:19.560 --> 23:23.560
The vanishing warmth

23:23.560 --> 23:27.500
I want to keep it here

23:27.500 --> 23:34.010
You, with your eyes closed

23:34.010 --> 23:37.940
Yearning over and over

23:37.940 --> 23:41.380
Even if I can't go anywhere

23:41.380 --> 23:45.420
When the heartache comes to a stop

23:45.420 --> 23:51.790
To the two of us, this moment is...

23:51.790 --> 23:56.790
...everything
